;_nc_gid=Xm5dOINVYx1eXFFITvw3zA&amp;_nc_ss=7020f&amp;oh=00_AQMEf2GyhGhqYJSHO5tagGIaIeq9IQOWLjLPENepRvYwzg&amp;oe=6ADEDEAD" alt="" /></div></div></a><div class="_amdc"><div class="_amdj">Research</div><div class="_amde"><a class="_amcw _amdf" aria-label="Read From Brain Waves to Words: Brain2Qwerty Offers a New Path to Communication Without Surgery" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/brain2qwerty-brain-ai-human-communication/" data-ms-clickable="true" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;click_internal-link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;latest-news-card-4&quot;&#125;" target="_self" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_c_HB">From Brain Waves to Words: Brain2Qwerty Offers a New Path to Communication Without Surgery</a></div><div class="_amdj">Jun 29, 2026</div></div></div></div></div><div class="_a5gf _a5gm _a5i9 _a5jn"></div><div class="_a5gf _a5gm _a5i9 _a5jn"></div><hr /><div><noscript id="u_0_d_R0"></noscript></div></div><noscript><div><div><h1 class="_8w6a _8w6b _8w61">Blog Posts</h1></div><div class="_7g--"><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">May 01, 2019</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Developer Tools</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">Open-sourcing new AI tools for adaptive experimentation</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">We are open-sourcing BoTorch and Ax, two new tools that leverage adaptive experimentation to efficiently tackle optimization challenges in tuning software configurations, machine learning hyperparameters, ranking systems, and more.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">May 01, 2019</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/open-sourcing-ax-and-botorch-new-ai-tools-for-adaptive-experimentation/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_e_9l"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">October 24, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">The Building Blocks of Agentic AI: From Kernels to Clusters</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">At PyTorch Conference 2025 in San Francisco, we unveiled five new projects spanning kernel languages, distributed systems, reinforcement learning, agentic frameworks, and edge AI deployment.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">October 24, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/introducing-pytorch-native-agentic-stack/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_f_Bl"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">August 05, 2024</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">Call for Applications: Llama 3.1 Impact Grants</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">We’re excited to begin accepting applications for the Llama 3.1 Impact Grants, the next iteration of a larger portfolio of work to support organizations as they pursue their ideas for how Llama can be used to address social challenges in their communities.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">August 05, 2024</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-3-1-impact-grants-call-for-applications/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_g_Cx"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">September 25, 2024</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">Connect 2024: The responsible approach we’re taking to generative AI </h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">With the rapidly evolving AI landscape, we recognize the importance of sharing our responsibility and safety approach with everyone.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">September 25, 2024</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/responsible-ai-connect-2024/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_h_hj"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">September 25, 2024</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Developer Tools</h4><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">Llama 3.2: Revolutionizing edge AI and vision with open, customizable models</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">Today, we’re releasing Llama 3.2, which includes small and medium-sized vision LLMs, and lightweight, text-only models that fit onto edge and mobile devices.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">September 25, 2024</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-3-2-connect-2024-vision-edge-mobile-devices/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_i_sq"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">April 29, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Developer Tools</h4><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">Sharing new open source protection tools and advancements in AI privacy and security </h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">Today, we’re releasing new Llama protection tools for the open source AI community.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">April 29, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/ai-defenders-program-llama-protection-tools/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_j_OG"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">August 27, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">How Llama and Oracle are helping Instituto PROA kickstart careers for students in Brazil</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">Instituto PROA, a nonprofit organization in Brazil, has transformed its job preparation process for young candidates by leveraging Llama and Oracle Cloud Infrastructure.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">August 27, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/llama-oracle-help-students-in-brazil/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_k_sz"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">August 14, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">DINOv3: Self-supervised learning for vision at unprecedented scale</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">DINOv3 scales self-supervised learning for images to create universal vision backbones that achieve absolute state-of-the-art performance across diverse domains, including web and satellite imagery.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">August 14, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/dinov3-self-supervised-vision-model/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_l_zR"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">August 14, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">Small robots, mighty vision: NASA Jet Propulsion Laboratory&#039;s DINOv2-enabled robot rovers and the future of planetary exploration</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">Using DINOv2, the team at NASA&#039;s Jet Propulsion Laboratory built a convenient robot operating system interface for robotic tasks.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">August 14, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/nasa-jpl-dino-robot-explorers/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_m_xU"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">August 14, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Research</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">How DINOv3 is helping World Resources Institute restore forests and farms globally</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">WRI and the Bezos Earth Fund used DINOv3 to develop an algorithm to accurately count individual trees from drone and satellite imagery.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">August 14, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xkm"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h"></p><div class="_8xko"><a class="_8xc5 _8x97 _8w61" href="https://ai.meta.com/blog/world-resources-institute-dinov3/" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;link&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;link&quot;&#125;" data-lnfb-mode="ie" id="u_0_n_wn"><span class="_8x6t _8x94 _8w61 _8w6h">Learn More</span><svg class="_8x95" fill="none" height="11" width="6" viewBox="0 0 6 10" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg"><path d="M1.22461 0.198869L5.78989 4.51989C6.07004 4.78505 6.07004 5.21495 5.78989 5.48011L1.22461 9.80113C0.944465 10.0663 0.490258 10.0663 0.21011 9.80113C-0.0700368 9.53597 -0.0700368 9.10606 0.21011 8.8409L3.19825 5.88451L4.15473 4.9792L3.19825 4.07389L0.21011 1.1591C-0.0700368 0.893936 -0.0700368 0.464029 0.21011 0.198869C0.490258 -0.0662898 0.944465 -0.0662898 1.22461 0.198869Z" fill="#344854"></path></svg></a></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div></div><div><div class="_8034"><div class="_8xm7" data-ms="&#123;&quot;creative&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;creative_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;,&quot;create_type_detail&quot;:&quot;listview-card&quot;&#125;"><div class="_8xis _8xhs"><div class="_8xm6"><div class="_8xm8"><p class="_8w6f _8w60 _8w6g">Blog</p></div><div class="_8xkp"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8wl0 _8w6h">August 07, 2025</p></div></div><div class="_8xiz"><div class="_8xit"><div class="_8wpy"><div class="_8x6u"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w60 _8xok _8x78">Open Source</h4></div></div><div class="_8wpz"><h4 class="_8w6a _8w6e _8w61">How Llama helps Biofy Technologies in the fight against antibiotic resistance</h4></div><div class="_8xkk"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8w61 _8w6h">Brazil, the biotech company Biofy Technologies has developed a groundbreaking platform using Llama that reduces diagnostic time for antibiotic resistance from five days to less than four hours.</p></div></div><div class="_8xix _8xiy"><div class="_8xkq"><div class="_8xkn"><p class="_8w6f _8xm4 _8wl0 _8w6h">August 0